Z||000000||Gottico||11-09-2000||10:28 PM||||88' Formula 5spd, Still having the same problems... Backfiring and no power in gear... Trans mount replacement in progress AGAIN (never trust a mechanic!!! 2 bolts missing, very twisted bracket). From all the advice I've gotten here and from other web sites, I believe it's the tach filter thats screwing things up... One problem though... What and where is the Tach filter????? Local parts stores (Pep Boy's, Auto Zone, etc) don't have any idea what it is... My assorted manuals make no referance to it. Only one person I know had heard of it and said it's on the distribtor... Only ignition and coil wires on mine.... HELP!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-10-2000||02:34 AM||||The tach filter is located by the dis. and coil. About 1 inch long and 1/2 to 3/4 inches in diameter, round with a couple of wires on it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||11-10-2000||08:03 AM||||Rodney Dickman has 'em. BTW does your tach read smoothly?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||11-10-2000||10:32 AM||||There should be a white plug, with white wires, somewhere near the bottom of the coil. Just unplug it. If the tach filter is the problem, the engine will now run smoothly. The tach will sit on zero.<P>Raydar||||reg||1
